        "says": "The context declares its field as the strategy interface, never a concrete strategy class.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Common Pitfalls and How to Avoid Them",
          "example:38-behavioral-patterns/README_9.3.1.md:3"
        ],
        "exercise": null,
        "reason": "the type of a field is a compile-time choice the given signatures already make, so no test result can differ; the sorter practice uses the interface throughout"
      },
      {
